https://docker-quick-reference.onrender.com

I deployed the Docker Quick Reference web application from exercise 1.15
to Render as a Web Service using the public Docker Hub image
jhlow0106/docker-quick-reference:latest. I selected the Free instance plan
and the Singapore region. The container runs a Python HTTP server as an
unprivileged user and listens on 0.0.0.0:8080. Render detected port 8080
and provides the public HTTPS endpoint. I configured /health as the
health check path and verified that it returns {"status": "ok"}. I also
opened the public home page and confirmed that the Docker command
reference is displayed. The deployment configuration is in render.yaml.

The free service spins down after 15 minutes without incoming traffic,
so the first request after an idle period can take about a minute.
